      "message": "Inlining av1_cost_tokens_from_cdf() makes real-time encodes much slower on x86 with clang-cl. In RT, coeff_cost_upd_level and mode_cost_upd_level stay at INTERNAL_COST_UPD_SB, so av1_fill_mode_rates() and av1_fill_coeff_costs() run for every superblock. With this inlined, av1_fill_mode_rates() grows from ~12 KB to ~21 KB of code (clang-cl 19.1.5).\n\nOn a Ryzen 9 5900X, speed 11, 1 thread, this CL alone takes the encode from 578 ms to 696 ms (+20%). AMD uProf shows the same instruction count and data access, but CPI in the cost fill code goes from 0.38 to 0.57-0.66, with 2-3x more op cache misses and 2x more L1 I-cache misses. Branch mispredicts are unchanged. Moving the function back to cost.c recovers it and stays bit exact. arm64 (M3 Pro) shows no difference either way. The unsigned av1_cost_symbol_clamped() change here is a win on x86, so I\u0027d keep that part.\n\nSuggested fix, which is what I measured: move av1_cost_tokens_from_cdf() back to cost.c as a normal function and keep only the declaration in cost.h, as before this CL. Removing the inline keyword is not enough, because a static function in the header still gets inlined. Please keep the unsigned av1_cost_symbol_clamped() change, it makes x86 3 to 6% faster.",
